1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:01,879
Your planet has more trees

2
00:00:01,879 --> 00:00:03,075
than your galaxy

3
00:00:03,075 --> 00:00:04,615
has STARS.

4
00:00:04,615 --> 00:00:06,167
And it's not close.

5
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,433
Trees win...

6
00:00:07,433 --> 00:00:09,780
at least SEVEN

7
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:10,800
to one.

8
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:11,778
Give every star

9
00:00:11,778 --> 00:00:12,688
in the Milky Way

10
00:00:12,688 --> 00:00:14,267
its own tree...

11
00:00:14,302 --> 00:00:15,915
and over two TRILLION

12
00:00:15,915 --> 00:00:18,133
trees still don't get one.

13
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,000
Funny thing?

14
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,386
Scientists used to think

15
00:00:20,386 --> 00:00:22,200
it was about a TIE.

16
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,690
Then someone counted...

17
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,067
from the GROUND.

18
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,870
Three TRILLION.

19
00:00:26,870 --> 00:00:28,180
And before farming?

20
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:29,867
Almost double that.

21
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:31,850
So, stargazers...

22
00:00:31,850 --> 00:00:32,490
you've been looking

23
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:33,986
the wrong way.

